   "en_span": "chapters/shiny_basics.qmd:149-149",
   "tr_span": "chapters/shiny_basics.ru.qmd:149-149",
   "proposition": "The Russian says the example app visualises data on the NUMBER OF MALARIA FACILITIES by district (данные о количестве малярийных учреждений); the English says it visualises malaria facility CASE-COUNT data (malaria_facility_count_data) by district, and the data used below has a cases_reported column, not a facility count.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Russian reader believes the dataset counts health facilities, so the epicurve of cases_reported and the age-group columns (malaria_rdt_0-4 etc.) make no sense against their mental model of the data.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Building a UI",
   "segment_index": "S9.P3",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/shiny_basics.qmd:217-217",
   "tr_span": "chapters/shiny_basics.ru.qmd:217-217",
   "proposition": "The Russian states that there are TWO identifiers (есть два идентификационных номера (ID)) used to pass information from the UI to the server; the English states that inputIds ARE the IDs used to pass information from the UI to the server, with no count of two.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Russian reader concludes a widget carries two IDs, or that a Shiny app has exactly two IDs, and then cannot make sense of the following requirement that IDs must be unique across a larger app with many widgets.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
